<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 15.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Feb 15.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Feb 15</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Reliance	     275	   1.00     416000 114.40    18.96</p>
<p>State Bank	   285	   1.03     392500 111.86    18.84</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   196	   0.72     443800  86.98    19.15</p>
<p>MTNL		   240	   0.87     230200  55.25    18.90</p>
<p>ITC		    420	   0.95     128300  53.89    11.79</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    345	   1.22     141800  48.92    18.44</p>
<p>ACC		   1415	   5.23	31130  44.05    19.27</p>
<p>Tata Power	   135	   0.49     306000  41.31    18.93</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    240	   0.85     160100  38.42    18.47</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   925	   2.61	38950  36.03    14.71</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 18.06 percent on an annualised basis against 19.15 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Feb 8.</p>
<p>The average badla charge takes into account the book-closure badla charges.The following scrip has gone into book - closure Castrol India Ltd.</p>
